# GoRun Design System

## System

GoRun uses one set of CSS-variable design tokens in `app/tokens.css`: light values on `:root`, dark overrides on the `.dark` class set by `next-themes`. Tailwind v4 exposes those tokens via `@theme inline` in `app/globals.css`. The brand action color `#2BC36B` is the only fixed value.

Do not reintroduce the old `--gr-*` system, `hsl(var(--...))` shadcn tuples, `.gr-dark`, `.gr-light`, or `tailwind.config.ts` color definitions.

## Hard Rules

- Never hardcode color in components, inline styles, or Tailwind arbitrary values. No hex, `rgb()`, `hsl()`, named colors, `bg-[#...]`, `text-[#...]`, or `border-[#...]`.
- Use token utilities (`bg-brand`, `text-ink`, `border-line`) or `var(--token)`.
- Never invent a token or color inline. If a new role is truly needed, add it to `app/tokens.css` for both `:root` and `.dark`, then expose it in `app/globals.css`.
- Dark mode is `.dark` only. Components should not need color-specific `dark:` logic.
- Green is for action/accent only: CTAs, logo mark, focus rings, progress fills, selected states, and positive-status pills. Never use brand green for body text, link text, or large neutral surfaces.
- Never put white text on bright brand green. Use `text-on-brand` on `bg-brand`; use `bg-brand-strong text-white` only when white text is truly required.
- Stop at four ink levels: `ink`, `ink-2`, `ink-3`, `ink-4`.
- Use only `rounded-sm`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`, and `rounded-[var(--r-pill)]` for pill buttons.
- Color is never the only signal. Status UI must include a label and/or icon.
- Inputs must be at least 16px (`text-base`). Every interactive element must show the `box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--brand-glow)` focus ring.

## Token Reference

- Brand/action: `brand`, `brand-hover`, `brand-active`, `brand-strong`, `brand-tint`, `on-brand`, `brand-glow`
- Surfaces: `bg`, `surface`, `surface-2`
- Borders: `line`, `line-strong`
- Text: `ink`, `ink-2`, `ink-3`, `ink-4`
- Status: `danger`, `danger-bg`, `warn`, `warn-bg`, `info`, `info-bg`, `success`, `success-bg`
- Ukraine accent: `afu-blue`, `afu-yellow`
- Elevation: `shadow-[var(--shadow-sm)]`, `shadow-[var(--shadow-md)]`, `shadow-[var(--shadow-lg)]`
- Radius: `r-sm`, `r-md`, `r-lg`, `r-xl`, `r-pill`
- Type: `font-display`, `font-sans`, `font-mono`

Legacy shadcn utilities (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-input`, etc.) still work through aliases. Prefer new GoRun utilities in any new or edited code.

## Variant primitive pattern

See `components/ui/button.tsx`. New primitives:

```tsx
const fooVariants = cva("base classes", {
  variants: {
    variant: { brand: "…", primary: "…", soft: "…" },
    size: {
      sm: "h-9 px-3.5 text-sm",
      md: "h-12 px-[18px] text-[15px]",
      lg: "h-14 px-[22px] text-base",
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: { variant: "brand", size: "md" },
});
```

- **GoRun variants** for NEW UI: `brand`, `primary`, `soft`, `ghost-gr`
- **Legacy shadcn variants** (`default`, `secondary`, `destructive`, `outline`, `ghost`, `link`) — kept for back-compat only
- **Sizes** are `sm | md | lg` (heights 9 / 12 / 14)

## Component Patterns

```tsx
<button className="min-h-11 rounded-[var(--r-pill)] bg-brand px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-on-brand shadow-[var(--shadow-sm)] hover:bg-brand-hover active:bg-brand-active focus-visible:shadow-[0_0_0_4px_var(--brand-glow)] focus-visible:outline-none">
  Register now
</button>

<input className="w-full rounded-md border border-line-strong bg-surface px-3.5 py-3 text-base text-ink placeholder:text-ink-4 focus:border-brand focus:shadow-[0_0_0_4px_var(--brand-glow)] focus:outline-none" />

<span className="rounded-[var(--r-pill)] bg-warn-bg px-2.5 py-1 text-sm font-semibold text-warn">
  Waitlist
</span>
```

## Anti-patterns

- Inline `style={{ ... }}` for anything that could be a utility or token
- Hardcoded colors or arbitrary color values
- `hsl(var(--...))`
- `.gr-dark`, `.gr-light`, or `--gr-*`
- White text on `bg-brand`
- Green text/links on light surfaces
- Skipping `cn()` and string-concatenating classNames
